        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:label>match algorithm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#matchesOutputPosition -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#matchesOutputPosition">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#TriggerRule"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Zero-based index of an output-region cell this rule requires to be non-zero.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>matches output position</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#mergeFormula -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#mergeFormula">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#ChainMergeTransformation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The transformation&apos;s definition over the collection x_1..x_n on the chain {0..k}, where k is the chain top. The chain analogue of re:assertedWhen: this is the definition, and an implementation is correct when it agrees with it. Integer arithmetic throughout — a fold that divides gives three runtimes three answers. PRECONDITION: every x_i lies in {0..k}. Closure depends on it and is not robust to its violation — strong-conjunction&apos;s bound sum(x_i) - k(n-1) &lt;= k holds only because each x_i &lt;= k, so feeding it cells above the declared k returns a value above the chain top (k=1 over [2,2] gives 3). What an engine should do when the precondition fails is deliberately not stated here.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>merge formula</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputAlphabetTop -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputAlphabetTop">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#PerceptualMapping"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger"/>
        <rdfs:comment>k, the top of the ordered chain {0..k} a machine&apos;s cells range over — absolute truth in the Lukasiewicz sense. Optional and undeclared across the corpus today. Required only for strong-disjunction and strong-conjunction, which are undefined without it: one clamps to k, and the other&apos;s closure bound holds only while every contribution is &lt;= k, so at the wrong k it yields a value outside both the chain and the machine&apos;s alphabet. Deliberately distinct from bitsPerElement, which gives the representable range rather than the alphabet — FallDetection declares 4 bits, representable 0..15, and ranges over {0..4}. meet, join and discrete-median take no k; join reads one only as an early-exit bound and answers the same with or without it.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>output alphabet top</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputConfidence -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputConfidence">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#Determination"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:label>output confidence</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputLength -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#outputLength">
