    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#requiresChainTop -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#requiresChainTop">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#OutputMergeTransformation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The transformation&apos;s result depends on k, the chain top, so k must be supplied for the fold to be defined. Where false the transformation may still accept k as an early-exit optimisation, but the answer is identical without it. See the UNRESOLVED note in the multi-valued commentary: k is not declared anywhere in the corpus today.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>requires chain top</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#requiresHumanApproval -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#requiresHumanApproval">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#AgentBinding"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:label>requires human approval</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#returnsAContributor -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#returnsAContributor">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#OutputMergeTransformation"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The result is always one of the collection&apos;s own values, so the fold cannot assert a level no completed Reality Event asserted. Strictly stronger than closure: bitwise or of 1 and 2 is 3, which is inside a chain {0..3} and asserted by nobody — on an ordinal severity ladder that invents a rung. False does not mean unsound; the Łukasiewicz operations combine evidence and are expected to land between contributors.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>returns a contributor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


