        <rdfs:label>Adolescent Mental Health Monitor — adolescent-mh-ok rule 1 (GREEN)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-behavioral-concern -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-behavioral-concern">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-elevated"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-elevated"/>
        <re:sequenceId>adolescent-mh-behavioral-concern</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires BEHAVIORAL_CONCERN when single-domain adversity (food insecurity OR unsafe housing but not both in crisis) is sustained alongside adolescent behavioral changes — the most common presentation requiring school-based mental health services in low-income districts.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Behavioral Concern: ELEVATED+ → BEHAVIORAL_CONCERN signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-crisis -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-crisis">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-stable"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-at-risk"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-stable"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-stressed"/>
        <re:sequenceId>adolescent-mh-crisis</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Detects adolescent mental health crisis driven by co-occurring food insecurity and housing instability — the dual adversity pathway most strongly linked to adolescent suicidality, substance use disorders, and school dropout in low-income populations. Requires STABLE+ baseline before crisis escalation arms. The 8D input vector reads four dimensions from each upstream machine, detecting simultaneous deterioration in both food security and housing safety.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Dual Adversity Crisis: STABLE+ → STRESSED → AT_RISK → CRISIS_RISK</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-ok -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#seq-adolescent-mh-ok">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-thriving"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/AdolescentMentalHealthMonitor#step-amh-thriving"/>
        <re:sequenceId>adolescent-mh-ok</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires MENTAL_HEALTH_OK when both upstream social determinant machines report stable/safe states and adolescent behavioral indicators are within normal range. Confirms that food and housing stability are supporting healthy adolescent development.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mental Health OK: THRIVING+ → MENTAL_HEALTH_OK signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


