        <re:outputMatchVector>0,0,0,0,1,0</re:outputMatchVector>
        <re:processStatus>warning</re:processStatus>
        <rdfs:comment>WELLNESS_CONCERN — patient observation by facilities staff raised welfare flag. Downstream: WellnessAnalytics longitudinal tracking.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>FacilitiesMaintenance — maint-wellness-concern rule 1 (AMBER)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-daily-routine -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-daily-routine">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-accessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-daily-done"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-hygiene-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-patient-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-space-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-dr-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-daily-routine</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Standard daily maintenance visit covering hygiene inspection, living space safety check, and patient observation. All conditions are within norms — visit completes with DAILY_COMPLETE logged. No clinical alerts generated. Visit documents: bathroom cleaned, linens acceptable, pathways clear, patient alert and responsive. Daily visits occur 5-7 days per week per facility policy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Daily Maintenance Routine — Normal Completion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-hygiene-concern -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-hygiene-concern">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-hc-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-hc-accessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-hc-hygiene-concern"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-hc-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-hygiene-concern</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Maintenance worker finds a hygiene deficit upon entering the unit: soiled or unchanged linens, uncleaned bathroom (soiling, odor, unflushed), depleted hygiene products, or evidence of incontinence-related hygiene failure. A concern is logged immediately — D7 rises while D2 stays LOW (hygiene not normal). HYGIENE_ALERT is written to perceptual space, feeding the DailyPatientCare machine&apos;s bathroom-nonuse detection path.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Hygiene Concern — Bathroom or Linen Deficit Observed</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-inaccessible -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-inaccessible">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-ia-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-ia-inaccessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-ia-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-inaccessible</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Maintenance worker is unable to enter the unit after multiple attempts. Patient does not respond to repeated knocking and announcements, and unit key is not producing a response (e.g., room appears occupied but no movement). After a facility-defined threshold (typically 2-3 attempts over 15-30 minutes), an inaccessibility concern is logged. INACCESSIBILITY_ALERT triggers emergency welfare check protocol — the patient may be unconscious, fallen, medically compromised, or (in community settings) may have eloped.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Unit Inaccessible — Welfare Check Threshold Reached</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-safety-concern -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-safety-concern">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#LifeSafetySequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-sc-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-sc-accessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-sc-hygiene-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-sc-space-concern"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-sc-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-safety-concern</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Maintenance worker finds a fall hazard or unsafe condition after hygiene inspection passes: loose rug or mat, displaced furniture creating a pathway obstruction, wet floor without signage, unsecured grab bar, cluttered walking area, or evidence of a recent fall (overturned furniture, items scattered on floor). D7 rises while D3 stays LOW (space not safe). SAFETY_ALERT feeds DailyPatientCare fall detection.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Safety Concern — Fall Hazard or Unsafe Condition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-weekly-deep-clean -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-weekly-deep-clean">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-accessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-deep-done"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-hygiene-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-nutrition-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-patient-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-space-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wd-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-weekly-deep-clean</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Weekly deep-clean visit covering all daily scope plus a full nutrition and hydration assessment. Includes: refrigerator inspection (food freshness, quantity), hydration supplies, pantry/snack inventory, complete linen change, and thorough bathroom deep clean. The nutrition dimension (D4) is exclusively assessed during weekly visits. Completes with WEEKLY_COMPLETE if all conditions are within norms.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Weekly Deep Clean — Full Inspection with Nutrition Assessment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-wellness-concern -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#seq-maint-wellness-concern">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-visit"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-accessible"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-hygiene-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-patient-concern"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-space-ok"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FacilitiesMaintenance#step-wc-visit"/>
        <re:sequenceId>maint-wellness-concern</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Maintenance worker encounters the patient during the visit and observes concerning behavior: failure to recognize familiar staff, disorientation to place, unusual affect (tearful, agitated, withdrawn, flat), apparent pain or distress, significant change from prior visit appearance, or failure to respond to greeting. D7 rises while D5 stays LOW (patient not observed normal). WELLNESS_CONCERN feeds WellnessAnalytics.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Wellness Concern — Patient Observation Raises Welfare Flag</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


