    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-confirmed -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-confirmed">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#LifeSafetySequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v2"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v3"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v4"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v5"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-conf-v6"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-confirmed</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>The only path that escalates to emergency dispatch. Six ticks of monotonic evidence are required: motion onset → sustained motion → severe motion → post-event stillness onset → sustained stillness → very-sustained stillness. Each transition is Hamming-distance 1, so a single anomalous tick (recovery, sensor noise) aborts the sequence and prevents an unwarranted RED dispatch.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Confirmed fall (motion → severe → sustained stillness) → RED</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-impact-recovered -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-impact-recovered">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-imprec-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-imprec-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-imprec-v2"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-imprec-v3"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-imprec-v4"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-impact-recovered</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Same motion-1→2→3 progression as &apos;sustained-instability&apos;, but the resident then returns to fully nominal. Log + suggest caregiver check-in. Note: this sequence runs in parallel with &apos;sustained-instability&apos; and only reaches its terminal output if the resident actually recovers; if they stay severe, only the AMBER-medium fires.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Severe motion that recovers → AMBER-high</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-intentional-lying -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-intentional-lying">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-intent-v"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-intent-v"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-intentional-lying</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Stillness-progression=2 reached without progressing through level 1 first (i.e., the resident chose to lie down). Logged at GREEN as &apos;intentional rest&apos; so the dashboard reflects current activity without any alert.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Intentional lying down (sustained stillness reached directly) → NOMINAL log</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-nominal -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-nominal">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-nominal-v"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-nominal-v"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-nominal</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>All-clear baseline. Fires every tick the sensor reports no motion progression and no stillness progression.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Nominal monitoring → GREEN</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-slow-collapse -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-slow-collapse">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#LifeSafetySequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-slow-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-slow-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-slow-v2"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-slow-v3"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-slow-collapse</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Catches the case where a resident slumps without struggle (syncope, stroke, cardiac event). Three ticks of monotonically increasing stillness with zero motion-progression. Lower confidence than the motion-validated path because silent stillness can also indicate intentional rest — the sequence requires the stillness signal to climb from 1→2→3, which is unusual for normal sleep transitions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Slow collapse / silent fall (no motion, escalating stillness) → RED</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-stumble-recovered -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-stumble-recovered">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-stumble-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-stumble-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-stumble-v2"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-stumble-recovered</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Single tick of motion-progression=1 followed by full recovery. Logged but not escalated.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Brief stumble (recovered in 2 ticks) → AMBER-low</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-sustained-instability -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#seq-fall-sustained-instability">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-sust-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-sust-v1"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-sust-v2"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/FallDetection#step-fall-sust-v3"/>
        <re:sequenceId>fall-sustained-instability</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Motion progression climbs across three ticks without a corresponding impact or recovery — caregiver should watch the resident.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sustained instability (motion 1→2→3 over 3 ticks) → AMBER-med</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


