    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-burnout-escalation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-burnout-escalation">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-coping"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-coping"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-high-burden"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-strained"/>
        <re:sequenceId>caregiver-burnout-escalation</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks caregiver burden escalation driven by simultaneous pediatric health and developmental challenges. When both upstream machines signal concern simultaneously, caregiver coping is overwhelmed — especially in single-parent, low-income households with no respite network. The COPING+ baseline requires at least one confirmed adequate period before burnout escalation can arm.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Burnout Cascade: COPING+ → STRAINED → HIGH_BURDEN_STATE → CAREGIVER_BURNOUT</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-coping-ok -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-coping-ok">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-managing"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-managing"/>
        <re:sequenceId>caregiver-coping-ok</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires CAREGIVER_COPING when both upstream child health machines report adequate states. Confirms that caregiver support systems and child health status are balanced — often reflecting successful WIC, Head Start, and home visiting program engagement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Caregiver Coping: MANAGING+ → CAREGIVER_COPING signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-high-burden -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#seq-caregiver-high-burden">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-burden"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeCaregiverBurdenMonitor#step-cb-burden"/>
        <re:sequenceId>caregiver-high-burden</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires HIGH_BURDEN when one upstream machine is in an alert state and the other is in concern state — the most common high-stress caregiver presentation, where one major child health issue compounds a second moderate concern. Common in WIC-enrolled families with a child in early intervention.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>High Burden: BURDEN+ → HIGH_BURDEN signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


