        <re:sourceFile>machines/domains/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor.json</re:sourceFile>
        <dcterms:description>Monitors primary biomarker control, symptom burden, self-management capacity, and lifestyle adherence for adults managing one or more chronic conditions (diabetes, hypertension, COPD, heart failure) at home in low- and medium-income settings. Poor chronic disease control in home care populations is driven by compounding social stressors rather than clinical non-compliance. Output at [2019:2022] feeds the Home Mental Health Access Monitor, reflecting the bidirectional chronic disease — depression comorbidity pathway.</dcterms:description>
