    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#rule-chronic-disease-poor-control-1 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#rule-chronic-disease-poor-control-1">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#TriggerRule"/>
        <re:appliesToSequence rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-poor-control"/>
        <re:hasRagStatus rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#AMBER"/>
        <re:matchesOutputPosition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</re:matchesOutputPosition>
        <re:outputMatchVector>0,1,0,0</re:outputMatchVector>
        <re:processStatus>warning</re:processStatus>
        <rdfs:comment>POOR_CONTROL: chronic disease consistently out of target range; complication risk elevated at [2019:2022]</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Home Chronic Disease Monitor — chronic-disease-poor-control rule 1 (AMBER)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-borderline -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-borderline">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-borderline"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-borderline"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-disease-borderline</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires BORDERLINE_CONTROL when disease metrics are in the near-miss zone — adequate enough to avoid acute events but insufficient for complication prevention. Common in working-poor patients managing diet and lifestyle without full access to chronic disease support programs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Borderline Control: BORDERLINE+ → BORDERLINE_CONTROL signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-controlled-ok -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-controlled-ok">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-well-controlled"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-well-controlled"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-disease-controlled-ok</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires DISEASE_CONTROLLED when biomarkers are in target range and self-management is functioning. In low-income home care, this outcome reflects successful care coordination and social barrier resolution — not just clinical compliance.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Disease Controlled: WELL_CONTROLLED+ → DISEASE_CONTROLLED signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-exacerbation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-exacerbation">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-controlled"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-controlled"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-exacerbation"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-poorly-controlled"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-slipping"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-disease-exacerbation</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks progressive chronic disease control loss leading to acute exacerbation. In home care settings, exacerbation events (diabetic ketoacidosis, hypertensive crisis, COPD exacerbation) are largely preventable with early monitoring. Social stressors — food insecurity, housing instability, caregiver burnout — are the predominant drivers of control loss in this population.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Disease Exacerbation: CONTROLLED+ → SLIPPING → POORLY_CONTROLLED → EXACERBATION → DISEASE_EXACERBATION</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-poor-control -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#seq-chronic-disease-poor-control">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-struggling"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicDiseaseMonitor#step-cd-struggling"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-disease-poor-control</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires POOR_CONTROL when chronic disease biomarkers are consistently out of target range without acute exacerbation — the sustained inadequate control state that drives long-term complications (retinopathy, nephropathy, peripheral vascular disease) in low-income diabetic and hypertensive populations.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Poor Control: STRUGGLING+ → POOR_CONTROL signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


