    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-crisis -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-crisis">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-managed"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-managed"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-severe"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-worsening"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-pain-crisis</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks progressive pain control failure toward functional crisis. In low-income home care, pain crisis episodes are often precipitated by medication access failures (opioid prior auth denied, pharmacy unable to fill, cost), weather-related flares, or loss of PT access. The MANAGED+ baseline confirms prior pain control before escalation can signal.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Pain Crisis: MANAGED+ → WORSENING → SEVERE → PAIN_CRISIS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-functional-impairment -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-functional-impairment">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-functionally-impaired"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-functionally-impaired"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-pain-functional-impairment</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires FUNCTIONAL_IMPAIRMENT when pain causes persistent ADL limitation without reaching crisis level. The largest chronic pain population segment — patients managing at home with significant daily function loss but not acute enough for emergency escalation. Drives depression, social withdrawal, and caregiver burden.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Functional Impairment: IMPAIRED+ → FUNCTIONAL_IMPAIRMENT signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-managed-ok -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-managed-ok">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-controlled"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-controlled"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-pain-managed-ok</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires PAIN_MANAGED when pain is adequately controlled, function maintained, opioid use stable, and activity preserved. In home care this reflects successful multimodal pain management — often the outcome of community health worker support combined with medication management.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Pain Managed: PAIN_CONTROLLED+ → PAIN_MANAGED signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-opioid-risk -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#seq-chronic-pain-opioid-risk">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-stable-rx"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-risk-signal"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeChronicPainMonitor#step-cp-stable-rx"/>
        <re:sequenceId>chronic-pain-opioid-risk</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks opioid risk escalation patterns — early refill requests, dose escalation without physician contact, sedation signs — in home care patients on prescribed opioids. Low-income patients are at higher opioid misuse risk due to untreated pain, mental health comorbidities, and limited alternative pain management access.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Opioid Risk: STABLE_RX+ → RISK_SIGNAL → OPIOID_RISK_ELEVATED</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


