    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-cost-adherence-crisis -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-cost-adherence-crisis">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-adherent"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-adherent"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-non-adherent"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-rationing"/>
        <re:sequenceId>med-cost-adherence-crisis</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks cost-driven medication adherence collapse. Patients who cannot afford medications first ration (splitting doses, skipping days), then stop refilling entirely. This sequence requires a confirmed ADHERENT baseline before the crisis escalation can arm — preventing false flags on patients who were never on medications.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Adherence Collapse: ADHERENT+ → RATIONING → NON_ADHERENT → ADHERENCE_CRISIS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-cost-barrier-active -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-cost-barrier-active">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-struggling"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-struggling"/>
        <re:sequenceId>med-cost-barrier-active</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires COST_BARRIER_ACTIVE when patient reports consistent cost barriers to medication access but has not yet reached full non-adherence. Targets the working-poor population managing chronic conditions on bare minimum insurance coverage or no coverage — the largest unserved medication access group.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Cost Barrier: STRUGGLING+ → COST_BARRIER_ACTIVE signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-managed -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#seq-med-managed">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-managed"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeMedicationCostBarrierMonitor#step-med-managed"/>
        <re:sequenceId>med-managed</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires MEDICATION_MANAGED when fill rates are adequate, adherence confirmed, and cost barriers resolved through generics, assistance programs, or insurance coverage. Represents successful pharmacy access navigation for a low-income patient.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Medication Managed: MANAGED+ → MEDICATION_MANAGED signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


