    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-connected-ok -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-connected-ok">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-stable"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-stable"/>
        <re:sequenceId>social-connected-ok</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires SOCIALLY_CONNECTED when both access barrier machines report adequate states — confirming that medication and transportation needs are met and the patient has resources to maintain social participation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Socially Connected: STABLE+ → SOCIALLY_CONNECTED signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-isolation-risk -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-isolation-risk">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-barrier-risk"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-barrier-risk"/>
        <re:sequenceId>social-isolation-risk</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Fires ISOLATION_RISK when one domain is in crisis state and the other is in a risk state — the early warning signal for patients who will become severely isolated if the second barrier is not addressed. Most responsive to outreach intervention before the full isolation cascade locks in.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Isolation Risk: BARRIER_RISK+ → ISOLATION_RISK signal</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-isolation-severe -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#seq-social-isolation-severe">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/ontology/re-core#CriticalEventSequence"/>
        <re:hasInitialStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-connected"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-connected"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-isolated"/>
        <re:hasStep rdf:resource="https://realityengine.example.org/machines/health-personal/HomeSocialIsolationMonitor#step-si-withdrawing"/>
        <re:sequenceId>social-isolation-severe</re:sequenceId>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracks progressive social isolation driven by compounding access barriers. When medication adherence crisis and transportation failure co-occur, the patient stops leaving the home, stops engaging community programs, and enters a self-reinforcing isolation spiral. Requires CONNECTED+ baseline before crisis arm activates.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Isolation Cascade: CONNECTED+ → WITHDRAWING → ISOLATED → SEVERE_ISOLATION</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


