        <dcterms:description>Monitors transportation access barriers that prevent low- and medium-income home health patients from attending medical appointments, filling prescriptions, and accessing community services. Transportation is a top driver of missed care in rural and low-income urban settings — more predictive of care gaps than insurance status alone. Output at [2015:2018] feeds the Home Social Isolation Monitor alongside the Medication Cost Barrier Monitor.</dcterms:description>
